---
import App from '../../layouts/App.astro';
import { faq } from '../../app/faq';

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: faq.map(({ q, a }) => ({ '@type': 'Question', name: q, acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: a } })),
};
---

<App
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
  title="About Badie"
  description="Badie finds badminton partners at your level, so you don’t have to ask strangers. Built by a player to get more people playing. Free to use."
>
  <h1 class="display text-5xl">About Badie</h1>
  <h2 class="text-2xl font-black">Why we built Badie</h2>
  <p class="max-w-prose text-lg">
    Badie began with its founder, who was too shy to walk up to strangers at the gym or ask for a game online. Even
    when a game came together, there was no telling whether the other side would be far better or just starting out.
  </p>
  <p class="max-w-prose text-lg">
    Plenty of players feel the same, so they play less than they’d like. Others lose their game when a regular partner
    can’t make it, or move somewhere new and don’t know anyone. In the US and Europe, where badminton communities are
    still small, that keeps courts quieter than they should be.
  </p>
  <p class="max-w-prose text-lg">
    So Badie does the finding for you. Tell it when you’re free and which courts you can reach, and it matches you with
    players at your level.
  </p>
  <p class="max-w-prose text-lg font-bold">Our goal: more people playing badminton in the US and Europe, more often.</p>
  <p class="max-w-prose">
    Badie is free to use. Court data comes from government open data, OpenStreetMap and players themselves.
  </p>
  <h2 class="text-2xl font-black">Questions</h2>
  {faq.map(({ q, a }) => (
    <section class="grid max-w-prose gap-1">
      <h3 class="text-lg font-black">{q}</h3>
      <p>{a}</p>
    </section>
  ))}
</App>
